1011	/**
1012	 * Valheim → container recreation with an --env-file (NOT a launch-args file).
1013	 *
1014	 * Found live 2026-09-06 by the catalog sweep, and this was the worst-behaved of
1015	 * the three pre-written apply functions: the previous version wrote a
1016	 * `nxeon-launch-args.txt` next to the server binary and returned **ok: true**,
1017	 * so the customer was notified "Game settings applied on <hostname>" while
1018	 * nothing on the server had changed and nothing ever read that file. Its own
1019	 * TODO admitted as much ("wire the start script/systemd unit to source this
1020	 * file") — but a TODO does not stop `ok: true` reaching a customer. Exactly the
1021	 * "asserting an outcome it never performed" failure this module's header calls
1022	 * out.
1023	 *
1024	 * The real mechanism, read off the running container's own
1025	 * `/usr/local/bin/valheim-server`:
1026	 *
1027	 *   "$valheim_server" -nographics -batchmode -name "$SERVER_NAME" \
1028	 *     -port "$SERVER_PORT" -world "$WORLD_NAME" -public "$SERVER_PUBLIC" \
1029	 *     "${valheim_server_args[@]}" $SERVER_ARGS
